A||N||6||kornholio||stalling when shifting into PARK again!!||||8||
Z||000000||kornholio||12-03-1999||09:10 PM||||Once in a while when I shift into park, my engine stalls.  It sometimes stalls when I shift into neutral too.  I thought I fixed this problem when I replaced the EGR valve and solenoid.  Could the EGR valve or solenoid be bad already?  How does a EGR solenoid go bad?  I've checked the EGR valve and it seems to be OK.  However, I don't know how to check the solenoid.  Any other suggestions on what would cause the stalling?<P>Also, if the torque convertor is not functioning, would it cause a hesitation when stepping on the gas from a stand still?  I did the "stepping on the brake" test on the highway and I didn't notice the RPM's increase.  How much of an increase should there be?  The reason I don't think that the torque convertor is bad is because I NEVER stall when I come to a stop at a stop light.<P>Thanks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||TOM||12-03-1999||10:33 PM||||Mine does that too sometimes. I was planing on checking the IAC||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||12-04-1999||02:20 AM||||TCC unlock is a couple hundred RPM. Pretty noticeable. It will kick back in once you  release the brake after about 2 seconds.<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-06-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-06-1999||12:32 PM||||Mine wouldn't actually stall when you put it in Park or Neutral, but it would stumble severely. I replaced the IAC valve, and the problem went away, briefly, only to return, several days later. Ended up disconnecting the battery to do some other stuff. Left it disconnected for several days. Since I reconnected it, I haven't seen the problem. As I understand it, disconnecting the battery (or pulling the fuse?) for just a few minutes (seconds?) should clear the ECM. But I didn't do it, the first time. <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-06-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||deceler8||12-06-1999||02:07 PM||||Is there  a way to reset the ECM other than by disconnecting the battery ?<P>If it's by pulling a fuse, which one ?||||reg||5
Z||000005||Raydar||12-08-1999||03:55 PM||||Seems like there is one (or two) fuse(s) labeled "ECM". Also might be the "guages" fuse. (This is from memory. I could be wrong. I know my Firebird was similar to this.) Be sure the key is off, before you do anything to drop power to the ECM. ECMs are smoke-operated devices. If you let the smoke out, they don't work any more.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||kornholio||12-08-1999||06:29 PM||||After cleaning the throttle body, I haven't stalled once when shifting into park or neutral!  So, people with this problem should look into this quick $5 fix first.||||reg||14
